        "cap": "2 triangles make a square. 2 squares make a rectangle. 6 triangles make a hexagon."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "Small shapes can fit together to make new, bigger shapes."
      },
      {
        "t": "why",
        "html": "When pieces fit with no gaps, the outside edge makes a new shape. You can trace the outside edge to name it."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Two triangles",
        "q": "What can two triangles that are the same make?",
        "steps": [
          "Put their long sides together.",
          "The outside edge has 4 sides and 4 square corners.",
          "It is a square (or a rectangle, if the triangles are long and thin)."
        ],
        "a": "A square or a rectangle"
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "<b>For grown-ups:</b> Cut a paper square from corner to corner and let your child put it back together. Then try making a big triangle with the same two pieces."
      },
